{
  "name": "Accessibility",
  "summary": "Visible focus, contrast in every mode, and signals beyond color.",
  "rules": [
    {
      "term": "Focus",
      "text": "Every interactive control has a focus variant (State = focus, or a combined -focus value) with a 2px focus/ring outline. It sits outside the control (3px) by default; inside for grid cells, header cells, and tabs, which touch their neighbours; and 1px inside the warning or error border on flagged cells, so both stay visible. The outline is its own layer, so focus never shifts the layout."
    },
    {
      "term": "Contrast in every mode",
      "text": "Text needs 4.5:1, and large text and UI graphics (icons, borders, focus rings) need 3:1 — in Light and Dark. Every pair a component uses is listed in tokens.json contrast.rules, and npm run contrast must pass. Disabled content is exempt (WCAG 1.4.3)."
    },
    …
